धिष्ठित a. standing, sticking;
 sitting on, being in
(loc. or acc.);
 being above or foremost;
 placed at the head of,
appointed to (loc. or —˚), founded on (loc.);
 inhabited, occupied,
seized, taken, filled, lead, managed, exercised (instr. or —˚).

धिष॑ण a. intelligent, wise;
 m. E. of Bṛhaspati. — f.
आ a cert. Soma-vessel, also fig. = the Soma-juice & its effects;
intelligence, wisdom, knowledge, a woman's name;
 du. the two worlds
(lit. bowls), i.e. heaven and earth;
 pl. heaven, earth, and air.

1 धि॑ष्ण्य a. spiritual, transcendental, holy, devout,
pious. — m. (f. आ & n.) a heap of earth, forming a sort of inferior
or side-altar;
 n. meteor (also f.);
 place, abode, region, star,
asterism.

2 धि॑ष्ण्य a. placed upon the earth-altar (v. prec.);
 m.
(±अग्नि) such a fire.
